{{Quote|I know the stories. My grandfather worked at an Imperial factory. Put food on the table when he couldn't find work anywhere else. Did that make him evil?|Tamara Ryvora|audio=TamGrandfather-TheNewTrooper.flac|<ref name="The New Trooper" />}}
The '''grandfather''' of the [[human]] [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Tamara Ryvora]] was a [[Gender|male]] individual who worked in an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[weapon]]s [[Unidentified Imperial factory|factory]]. In [[34 ABY]], Ryvora told the [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] and the mechanic [[Jarek Yeager]] about her grandfather's occupation and how it had assisted her [[Tamara Ryvora's family|family]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|You're just too young to understand, Tam. The Empire exploited the vulnerable that&mdash;''"<br />"''Oh, I understand. I understand that you're taking Kaz's side. Again.|Jarek Yeager and Tamara Ryvora, after the latter discussed her grandfather's past|audio=JarekTam-TheNewTrooper.flac|<ref name="The New Trooper" />}}
[[File:TamaraRyvora-LiveFire.jpg|thumb|right|260px|The man was the grandfather of Tamara Ryvora (pictured).]]
A [[Gender|male]] individual who eventually became the grandfather of the [[human]] [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Tamara Ryvora]] lived during the [[Imperial Era]]. During this time, he worked in a [[Unidentified Imperial factory|factory]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]. Though he searched elsewhere for work, laboring in<ref name="The New Trooper" /> the [[weapons factory]]<ref name="Interview">{{WookYouTube|ML1nYpSU0d0|Wookieepedia Interviews - Brandon Auman}}</ref> proved to be the only way to [[Foodstuff|feed]] his [[Tamara Ryvora's family|family]].<ref name="The New Trooper" /> At some point after he had stopped working there,<ref name="Interview" /> Ryvora was informed of<ref name="The New Trooper" /> her<ref name="Minds Behind">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-resistance-final-season-interview|text=The Minds Behind ''Star Wars Resistance'' on What's Ahead in the Final Season}}</ref> grandfather's Imperial employment and how it had assisted her family.<ref name="The New Trooper" />

While aboard the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|supertanker fuel depot]] ''[[Colossus]]''<ref name="The New Trooper" /> in [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{ResistanceDate|1|16}}</ref> Ryvora felt comforted<ref name="The New Trooper" /> by the arrival of the Empire's successor state,<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> the [[First Order]], and its [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] presence because they reminded the mechanic of her grandfather's past. She discussed the First Order's arrival on the ''Colossus'' with [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] and mechanic [[Jarek Yeager]], both of whom felt that the loss of autonomy resulting from the outsiders' control was reminiscent of Imperial [[Dictatorship|tyranny]]. Ryvora disagreed, informing the pair of her grandfather's former employment and surmising that not everyone working for the Empire had harbored evil intent. Though Yeager attempted to explain that Imperials had exploited vulnerable individuals, she scoffed and left.<ref name="The New Trooper" />

==Personality and traits==
After unsuccessfully searching for work elsewhere, the grandfather acquiesced to working in an Imperial [[weapon]]s [[factory]] in order to keep his family fed.<ref name="The New Trooper" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Tam's background&mdash;her grandfather worked for the Empire&mdash;means that she doesn't view the Empire as bad.|Justin Ridge|<ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|194|Switching Sides}}</ref>}}
[[File:StarWarsResistance-SeasonOne.jpg|thumb|right|190px|The grandfather was introduced via mention in ''Star Wars Resistance''{{'s}} first season.]]
Tamara Ryvora's grandfather was first mentioned in "[[The New Trooper]],"<ref name="The New Trooper" /> the sixteenth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated television series,<ref name="Insider 190">{{InsiderCite|190|Resistance Revisited|''Resistance'' Revisited}}</ref> which premiered on [[November 4]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> ''Resistance'' executive producer [[Justin Ridge]]<ref name="The New Trooper" /> felt that having Ryvora discuss her grandfather's past on the show was important,<ref name="Minds Behind" /> as it explained why she did not view the Empire as inherently evil.<ref name="Insider" />

Another of the show's executive producers, [[Brandon Auman]], noted the significance of Ryvora being too young to truly understand the Empire's evils as she had not been alive during its reign. Instead, Auman felt that she only comprehended that good people had been able to earn a living and support their families by working for Imperials, without also realizing that the work done in the Empire's factories&mdash;such as the one that employed her grandfather&mdash;often produced weapons of war.<ref name="Interview" />

